    <!-- Slideshow. The same preferences the viewer's 幻灯片 row edits - one interval and one
         order, two doors. The viewer is where they are usually changed, but a slideshow is
         often set up before anyone is looking at a photo, and reaching that row means
         opening a picture and pressing 幻灯片 first. -->
    <string name="settings_slideshow_interval_hint">How long each photo stays on screen.</string>
    <string name="settings_slideshow_order_hint">In order walks the list; shuffle draws from every photo. A show only ever plays photos — videos are stepped over.</string>
    <string name="settings_slideshow_music">Background music</string>
    <string name="settings_slideshow_same_hint">The same value as the 幻灯片 control bar in the viewer; changing it in either place changes both.</string>

